OL,3,GNEWSAHot chilli legacy of summer
OL,4,Aheatwave
OL,5,
OL,6,FAn amateur gardener has produced a
OL,7,Fbumper crop of chillies - boosted by
OL,8,Fthe scorching hot summer.
OL,10,FJeremy Crumb from Stoke Gifford near
OL,11,FBristol only began growing the South
OL,12,FAmerican plants a few years ago but now
OL,13,Ftends dozens of varieties in his small
OL,14,Fback garden.
OL,16,FHe said: "What's been very interesting
OL,17,Fthis year, is normally it's the plants
OL,18,Fin the greenhouse that flourish, but
OL,19,Fbecause of the very hot summer even the
OL,20,Fones outside are healthy and absolutely
OL,21,Fstacked out with fruit.
OL,23,APub: 24-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,343,340,200,160,0,100
